year and a half ago for a health review before
renewing his driver''s license. Your examination
revealed 6/24 vision for both eyes; therefore,
you advised that he should not drive anymore
and encouraged him to self-report to licensing
authorities and be referred for assessment by
an ophthalmologist. Today, he presented again
and asked if you could change your mind and
give him a letter so that he could drive. You
examine him again and realise he still has poor
eyesight and is unfit to drive. When you tell him
so, he becomes irritated and says that he saw
another doctor who gave him a letter last year
and has been driving since then. why do you
not just give him a similar letter as well? Which
of the following is the most appropriate action
now that you know him driving despite his
unfitness to drive?','{"A":"the police.","B":"Call the doctor who issued the\nletter and ask him why he has done\nSO.","C":"Report the patient to the relevant\nRoad and Traffic department.","D":"Ask him to drive only if there is\nsomeone else in the car to\nSupervise him.","E":"It is not your duty to report him to\nanyone. Tell him again that he is\nunfit to drive and must submit his\nlicense to authorities."}','E',NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Public health  (3).pdf","supporting_pages":[4,5],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-d4d221c5dc9d","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"2a40fa39af2781166bf5","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Public health  (3).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Public health  (3).pdf","source_page":4,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_cross_page_option_stitch","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"2a40fa39af2781166bf5","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Public health  (3).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Public health  (3).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":4,"supporting_pages":[4,5],"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Ethics/Population Health","stem":"Steven is a 67-year-old patient who presented a\nyear and a half ago for a health review before\nrenewing his driver''s license. Your examination\nrevealed 6/24 vision for both eyes; therefore,\nyou advised that he should not drive anymore\nand encouraged him to self-report to licensing\nauthorities and be referred for assessment by\nan ophthalmologist. Today, he presented again\nand asked if you could change your mind and\ngive him a letter so that he could drive. You\nexamine him again and realise he still has poor\neyesight and is unfit to drive. When you tell him\nso, he becomes irritated and says th