asthma presents with a severe attack of
asthma following an upper respiratory
infection. On physical examination, he
appears distressed with a pulse rate of 130
bpm, respiratory rate of 48 breaths per
minute and temperature of 37.1°C. Bedside
pulse oximetry shows an oxygen saturation
of 85% while on room air. Which one of the
following is the most appropriate initial step
in management?','{"A":"Give salbutamol inhalation and\nrecommend salbutamol inhaler 4-\nhourly at home and review in 24\nhours.","B":"Start 4-hourly salbutamol and\nipratropium bromide inhalers and\nOral prednisolone, and review in 24\nhours.","C":"Start inhaled salbutamol and oral\namoxicillin 4-hourly, and review in\n24 hours.","D":"Give oxygen and continuous\nSalbutamol inhalations and transfer\nto the hospital by ambulance.","E":"Refer for admission to the hospital\nfor salbutamol and ipratropium\ninhalations."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Respiratory  (1).pdf","supporting_pages":[78,79],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-8c57893a9866","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"b359e5a1e4cd68243af0","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Respiratory  (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Respiratory  (1).pdf","source_page":78,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_cross_page_option_stitch","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"b359e5a1e4cd68243af0","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Respiratory  (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Respiratory  (1).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":78,"supporting_pages":[78,79],"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Respiratory","stem":"A 4-year-old boy with a background history of\nasthma presents with a severe attack of\nasthma following an upper respiratory\ninfection. On physical examination, he\nappears distressed with a pulse rate of 130\nbpm, respiratory rate of 48 breaths per\nminute and temperature of 37.1°C. Bedside\npulse oximetry shows an oxygen saturation\nof 85% while on room air. Which one of the\nfollowing is the most appropriate initial step\nin management?","options":{"A":"Give salbutamol inhalation and\nrecommend salbutamol inhal