chronic obstructive pulmonary disease
(COPD), presents to the emergency
department with severe shortness of breath
and cough. Based on the diagnosis of a COPD
exacerbation, he is started on oxygen 28% by
Venturi mask. After one hour, an ABG is
obtained, showing a PaO2 of 42mmHg anda
PaCO2 of 68mmHg. Which one of the
following is the next best step in
management?','{"A":"Increase the oxygen flow and use\nface mask.","B":"Assisted ventilation.","C":"Decrease the oxygen flow.","D":"Continue with the same amount of\noxygen and repeat the ABG after\none hour.","E":"Add inhaled short-acting B2\nagonists."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Respiratory  (1).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-28860cfd1518","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"1d6c65efad6b3d75f97c","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Respiratory  (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Respiratory  (1).pdf","source_page":111,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"1d6c65efad6b3d75f97c","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Respiratory  (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Respiratory  (1).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":111,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Respiratory","stem":"A 72-year-old man, who is a known case of\nchronic obstructive pulmonary disease\n(COPD), presents to the emergency\ndepartment with severe shortness of breath\nand cough. Based on the diagnosis of a COPD\nexacerbation, he is started on oxygen 28% by\nVenturi mask. After one hour, an ABG is\nobtained, showing a PaO2 of 42mmHg anda\nPaCO2 of 68mmHg. Which one of the\nfollowing is the next best step in\nmanagement?","options":{"A":"Increase the oxygen flow and use\nface mask.","B":"Assisted ventilation.","C":"Decrease the oxygen flow.","D":"Continue with the same amount of\noxygen and repeat the ABG after\none hour.","E":"Add inhaled short-acting B2\nagonists."},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","c