Department with complaints of cough, fever,
joint pain, and malaise for the past few days.
He denies night sweats, weight loss, and
chills. He does not smoke. On examination,
painful raised erythematosus rashes are
observed over his anterior tibia. The rest of
the physical exam is inconclusive. A chest X-
ray is done that shows bilateral hilar
lymphadenopathy. Which one of the
