with a complaint of cough. His mother
explains that the cough started 2 months ago
and sometimes wakes him up at night. He
also has them when he plays with other
children or runs, and sometimes is associated
with a small amount of clear phlegm. On
history, you learn that he had flexural
eczema when he was 2 years old. Their child
is afebrile. On chest examination, no wheeze
is heard. The rest of the physical exam is
inconclusive. Which one of the following is
the most likely diagnosis?','{"A":"Epiglottitis.","B":"Chronic sinusitis.","C":"Asthma.","D":"Gastro-esophageal reflux disease.","E":"Whooping cough."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Respiratory  (2).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-1f168cb3fe03","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"5455e9894b2d2f110868","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Respiratory  (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Respiratory  (2).pdf","source_page":48,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','low','{"record_id":"5455e9894b2d2f110868","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Respiratory  (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Respiratory  (2).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":48,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Respiratory","stem":"A 5-year-old child is brought to your clinic\nwith a complaint of cough. His mother\nexplains that the cough started 2 months ago\nand sometimes wakes him up at night. He\nalso has them when he plays with other\nchildren or runs, and sometimes is associated\nwith a small amount of clear phlegm. On\nhistory, you learn that he had flexural\neczema when he was 2 years old. Their child\nis afebrile. On chest examination, no wheeze\nis heard. The rest of the physical exam is\ninconclusive. Which one of the following is\nthe most likely diagnosis?","options":{"A":"Epiglottitis.","B":"Chronic sinusitis.","C":"Asthma.","D":"Gastro-esophageal reflux disease.","E":"Whooping cough."},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"low","currentness_keywords":[],"likely_visual_question"