emergency department by paramedics
because of severe shortness of breath. Upon
arrival, a bedside pulse oxymetry showed an
O2 saturation of 85% in room air. His son
States that this is the fifth time he has been
admitted to the emergency department due
to the same problem. On further inquiry, he
is found to have smoked 60 packs per year
for the past 30 years. He is given oxygen 28%
by Venturi mask. Thirty minutes later, an
arterial blood gas (ABG) reports his PaO2 and
PaCO2 68 mmHg and 60 mmHg, respectively.
The O2 saturation is 88% while on oxygen.
